# CSS Scoping & Architecture Rules

## Purpose and Scope

This rule enforces mandatory CSS Modules scoping and component-based CSS architecture. It ensures that all component styles are properly scoped, prevents global CSS conflicts, and maintains a clean, predictable styling system. The rule establishes clear file naming conventions, CSS architecture layers, and implementation patterns for consistent styling across the application.

## Standards and Requirements

### CSS Module Scoping - MANDATORY
- Every React component MUST have a corresponding .module.css file
- Component styles MUST be imported as: `import styles from './Component.module.css'`
- All className attributes MUST use the styles object: `className={styles.className}`
- NEVER mix CSS Modules with global CSS classes in the same component

### File Naming Conventions
- Component files: `ComponentName.jsx`
- CSS Module files: `ComponentName.module.css`
- Global CSS files: `globals.css`, `variables.css` (in src/styles/)

### CSS Module Class Naming
- Use camelCase: `.headerRow`, `.beerCard`, `.sectionTitle`
- Be specific to the component: `.cardTitle` not `.title`
- Use semantic names: `.primaryButton` not `.blueButton`

### CSS Architecture Layers
1. **Global Layer** (`src/styles/globals.css`):
   - CSS resets only
   - Typography base styles
   - CSS custom properties (:root)
   
2. **Component Layer** (`.module.css` files):
   - ALL component-specific styles
   - Layout within the component
   - Component variants and states

### Prohibited Global CSS
- NO component layouts in global CSS
- NO color values (use CSS custom properties)
- NO spacing values (use CSS custom properties)
- NO utility classes (use CSS Modules)

## Examples

### Good Examples

```css
/* Component.module.css */
.component {
  padding: var(--spacing-lg);
  background: var(--color-background);
  border-radius: var(--border-radius);
}

.title {
  font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
  color: var(--color-primary);
  margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
}

.content {
  font-size: var(--font-size-base);
  line-height: 1.6;
}
```

```javascript
// CORRECT - CSS Modules
import styles from './Component.module.css';

export function Component({ variant = 'default' }) {
  const componentClass = variant === 'primary' 
    ? styles.componentPrimary 
    : styles.component;
    
  return (
    <div className={componentClass}>
      <h2 className={styles.title}>Title</h2>
      <div className={styles.content}>Content</div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

```css
/* globals.css - ONLY place for these */
:root {
  /* Colors */
  --color-primary: #1a4d5c;
  --color-secondary: #d4af37;
  --color-background: #ffffff;
  --color-text: #333333;
  
  /* Spacing */
  --spacing-xs: 0.25rem;
  --spacing-sm: 0.5rem;
  --spacing-md: 1rem;
  --spacing-lg: 2rem;
  --spacing-xl: 4rem;
}
```

### Bad Examples

```javascript
// INCORRECT - Global classes
export function Component() {
  return (
    <div className="component"> {/* ❌ Global class */}
      <h2 className="title">Title</h2> {/* ❌ Global class */}
    </div>
  );
}
```
*Fails: Uses global CSS classes instead of CSS Modules scoping.*

```css
/* INCORRECT - Component styles in global CSS */
.component {
  padding: 1rem;
  background: white;
  border-radius: 8px;
}
```
*Fails: Component-specific styles should be in CSS Modules, not global CSS.*

```css
/* INCORRECT - Hardcoded values */
.button {
  background: #1a4d5c; /* ❌ Hardcoded color */
  padding: 16px; /* ❌ Hardcoded spacing */
}
```
*Fails: Uses hardcoded values instead of CSS custom properties.*

## Implementation Guidelines

### CSS Custom Properties Strategy
```css
/* globals.css - ONLY place for these */
:root {
  /* Colors */
  --color-primary: #1a4d5c;
  --color-secondary: #d4af37;
  --color-background: #ffffff;
  --color-text: #333333;
  
  /* Spacing */
  --spacing-xs: 0.25rem;
  --spacing-sm: 0.5rem;
  --spacing-md: 1rem;
  --spacing-lg: 2rem;
  --spacing-xl: 4rem;
  
  /* Typography */
  --font-family: 'Arial', sans-serif;
  --font-size-sm: 0.875rem;
  --font-size-base: 1rem;
  --font-size-lg: 1.25rem;
  --font-size-xl: 2rem;
  
  /* Layout */
  --container-max-width: 1200px;
  --border-radius: 8px;
  --transition-speed: 0.3s;
  
  /* Z-index scale */
  --z-dropdown: 100;
  --z-modal: 1000;
  --z-header: 1100;
}
```

### Component CSS Structure Template
```css
/* Component.module.css */

/* Main component wrapper */
.component {
  /* Use variables for consistency */
  padding: var(--spacing-lg);
  background: var(--color-background);
  border-radius: var(--border-radius);
}

/* Child elements */
.title {
  font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
  color: var(--color-primary);
  margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
}

.content {
  font-size: var(--font-size-base);
  line-height: 1.6;
}

/* States */
.component:hover {
  transform: translateY(-2px);
  transition: transform var(--transition-speed) ease;
}

/* Variants */
.componentPrimary {
  background: var(--color-primary);
  color: white;
}

.componentSecondary {
  background: var(--color-secondary);
  color: white;
}

/* Responsive */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .component {
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  
  .title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
  }
}
```

### CSS Module Composition (Advanced)
```css
/* Base.module.css */
.button {
  padding: var(--spacing-sm) var(--spacing-md);
  border: none;
  border-radius: var(--border-radius);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: all var(--transition-speed) ease;
}

/* Button.module.css */
.primaryButton {
  composes: button from './Base.module.css';
  background: var(--color-primary);
  color: white;
}

.secondaryButton {
  composes: button from './Base.module.css';
  background: var(--color-secondary);
  color: white;
}
```

### Debugging CSS Modules
- Use browser dev tools to see generated class names
- Check that styles object contains expected properties
- Verify import paths are correct
- Ensure .module.css files are in the same directory as components

### Code Review Checklist
- [ ] Component has corresponding .module.css file
- [ ] All styles imported using CSS Modules syntax
- [ ] No global CSS classes used in component JSX
- [ ] CSS custom properties used instead of hardcoded values
- [ ] No !important declarations
- [ ] Responsive design implemented with mobile-first approach
- [ ] Semantic class names used
- [ ] Proper CSS property ordering followed

